    "slug": "tax-matters-in-pakistan-05-ultimate-doctrine",
    "title": "Tax Matters in Pakistan 05 Ultimate Doctrine of Past and Closed Transactions",
    "excerpt": "I. Introduction A. Definition of the Doctrine:    The doctrine of past and closed transactions in tax matters refers to a principle in taxation that provides legal protection to taxpayers against the reassessment or reopening of tax assessments for a particular period once the time for such review has expired. In essence, it establishes a Continue reading",
